## Code Snippets

While reviewing the other parts of the codebase, I came across a snippet in the `userService.js` that could be refactored for clarity:

```javascript
function getUserById(userId) {
    return database.query(`SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = ?`, [userId])
        .then(result => {
            if (result.length > 0) {
                return result[0];
            }
            throw new Error('User not found');
        });
}
```

It might be worthwhile to implement async/await for better readability:

```javascript
async function getUserById(userId) {
    const result = await database.query(`SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = ?`, [userId]);
    if (result.length > 0) {
        return result[0];
    }
    throw new Error('User not found');
}
```

This change improves the readability and maintainability of the code, making it easier for future developers to understand.

